<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;YURIY SARANTSEV&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yuriy Sarantsev is a talented young actor born and raised in the Soviet Union, known for his charismatic performances and significant contributions to Soviet cinema."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOVIET UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Soviet Union is the primary setting and context for Yuriy Sarantsev's life and career, emphasizing its role in nurturing his artistic growth and providing access to arts education."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUSSIAN REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Russian Revolution is a pivotal historical event that marks the beginning of the Soviet Union, shaping its early years and the political climate."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPSON'S-IN-THE-STRAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Simpson's-in-the-Strand is a London restaurant where Yuriy Sarantsev frequently dines, symbolizing his integration into British society."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRS. PEMBERTON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mrs. Pemberton is Yuriy Sarantsev's agent, a key figure in his professional life, responsible for securing roles and opportunities for him."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL SHAKESPEARE COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Shakespeare Company is an esteemed British theatrical organization that expresses interest in casting Yuriy Sarantsev in a lead role."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAMLET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hamlet is the role Yuriy Sarantsev is offered by the Royal Shakespeare Company, representing a significant opportunity in his acting career."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London is the city where Yuriy Sarantsev has lived and worked, becoming an adopted homeland for him."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED KINGDOM OF GREAT BRITAIN AND IRELAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland is the country that has provided Yuriy Sarantsev with opportunities and a sense of belonging."&lt;SEP&gt;"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland is the country that took Yuriy in and provided him with opportunities, symbolizing a place of refuge and growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AND QUIET FLOWS THE DON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"And Quiet Flows the Don is a critically acclaimed production of Mikhail Sholokhov's novel, showcasing Yuriy Sarantsev's talent and reputation in Soviet cinema."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAR AND PEACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"War and Peace is a film in which Yuriy Sarantsev starred, cementing his status as a leading man of Soviet cinema."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEY FOUGHT FOR THEIR COUNTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"They Fought for Their Country is another film in which Yuriy Sarantsev starred, further establishing his reputation in Soviet cinema."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOVIET ACTORS' UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Soviet Actors' Union is an organization Yuriy Sarantsev was an active member of, using his platform to promote socialist values and international cooperation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CULTURAL EXCHANGE PROGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cultural exchange programs, including tours of Eastern Europe and Cuba, are activities Yuriy Sarantsev participated in, further solidifying his connection to the Soviet state."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THAMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Thames is the river off which the fog rolls in, setting the scene for Yuriy Sarantsev's visit to Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EMERALD GREEN HAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"An emerald green hat is part of Mrs. Pemberton's attire, described as she greets Yuriy Sarantsev at Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLARET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Claret is a type of wine that Yuriy Sarantsev enjoys with his meal at Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FOG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fog is a weather condition that sets the scene for Yuriy Sarantsev's arrival at Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROAST BEEF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Roast beef is a dish that Yuriy Sarantsev enjoys at Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOFT MURMUR OF CONVERSATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soft murmur of conversation is a sound that blends with the ambiance of Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLINKING OF GLASSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"OBJECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Clinking of glasses is a sound that blends with the ambiance of Simpson's-in-the-Strand."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YURIY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yuriy feels a deep sense of pride and gratitude towards the United Kingdom, indicating a strong emotional connection and appreciation."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ELEGANCE AND REFINEMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"British elegance and refinement are the cultural and social aspects that Yuriy appreciates and feels proud of."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITIZEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citizen refers to Yuriy's status as a member of the United Kingdom, highlighting his integration and belonging."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPPORTUNITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Opportunities refer to the chances and prospects that the United Kingdom provided Yuriy, emphasizing the positive impact on his life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0369</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;YURIY SARANTSEV&quot;" target="&quot;SOVIET UNION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Yuriy Sarantsev's life and career are deeply intertwined with the Soviet Union, which nurtured his artistic growth and provided access to arts education."</data>
      <data key="d5">"nurturing, artistic growth"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;YURIY SARANTSEV&quot;" target="&quot;RUSSIAN REVOLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"The Russian Revolution marks the beginning of the Soviet Union, which shaped the political and cultural environment in which Yuriy Sarantsev grew up and pursued his career."</data>
      <data key="d5">"political climate, cultural environment"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;YURIY SARANTSEV&quot;" target="&quot;SIMPSON'S-IN-THE-STRAND&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Yuriy Sarantsev frequently dines at Simpson's-in-the-Strand, symbolizing his integration into British society and his adopted homeland."</data>
      <data key="d5">"integration, adopted homeland"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0369</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;YURIY SARANTSEV&quot;" target="&quot;MRS. PEMBERTON&quot;">
